    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits the use of 'fingerprints or'",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Omit ‘fingerprints or’",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Substitute ‘fingerprints and/or’"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 After subsection 3ZL(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(3A) The judge or magistrate may also make any other orders that are\nreasonably necessary for ensuring that the impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or a photograph of the person are taken in\naccordance with the order under subsection (1). For example, the\njudge or magistrate may order the person to attend a specified\npolice station at a specified time.\n\n(3B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under subsection (3A); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(3C) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(3A) The judge or magistrate may also make any other orders that are\nreasonably necessary for ensuring that the impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or a photograph of the person are taken in\naccordance with the order under subsection (1). For example, the\njudge or magistrate may order the person to attend a specified\npolice station at a specified time.\n\n(3B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under subsection (3A); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(3C) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-2-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-2-ss-3b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-2-ss-3c"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 After subsection 3ZL(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(3A) The judge or magistrate may also make any other orders that are\nreasonably necessary for ensuring that the impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or a photograph of the person are taken in\naccordance with the order under subsection (1). For example, the\njudge or magistrate may order the person to attend a specified\npolice station at a specified time.\n\n(3B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under subsection (3A); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(3C) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914"
    },
