    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-4ja",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4JA Some indictable offences punishable by fine only may be dealt",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-4ja"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "with summarily\n\n(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.\n\n(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary\npenalty of:\n\n(a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty\nunits for a body corporate; or\n\n(b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty\nunits for a body corporate.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914",
      "skos:definition": "with summarily\n\n(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.\n\n(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary\npenalty of:\n\n(a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty\nunits for a body corporate; or\n\n(b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty\nunits for a body corporate.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-4ja-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-4ja-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eea591ee022001839297adbf7f7411706dc348815a08e89e6130150777121555"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-4ja",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4JA Some indictable offences punishable by fine only may be dealt",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "with summarily\n\n(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.\n\n(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary\npenalty of:\n\n(a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty\nunits for a body corporate; or\n\n(b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty\nunits for a body corporate.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-4ja-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4JA(1) Some indictable offences punishable by fine only may be dealt",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-4ja-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.",
      "values:partOf": {
