        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7D Subsection 23YUD(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-7d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into\narrangements with a responsible Minister of a participating\njurisdiction under which:\n\n(a) information from the DNA database system of the\nCommonwealth that may be relevant to the investigation of a\nmatter relating to the participating jurisdiction is to be\ntransmitted to the appropriate authority in that jurisdiction for\nthe purpose of the investigation of, or proceedings in respect\nof, that matter; and\n\n(b) information from a DNA database system of the participating\njurisdiction that may be relevant to the investigation of a\nmatter relating to the Commonwealth is to be transmitted to\nthe Commissioner for the purposes of the investigation of, or\nproceedings in respect of, that matter.\nThese arrangements may deal with keeping, and otherwise\nmanaging, such information.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into\narrangements with a responsible Minister of a participating\njurisdiction under which:\n\n(a) information from the DNA database system of the\nCommonwealth that may be relevant to the investigation of a\nmatter relating to the participating jurisdiction is to be\ntransmitted to the appropriate authority in that jurisdiction for\nthe purpose of the investigation of, or proceedings in respect\nof, that matter; and\n\n(b) information from a DNA database system of the participating\njurisdiction that may be relevant to the investigation of a\nmatter relating to the Commonwealth is to be transmitted to\nthe Commissioner for the purposes of the investigation of, or\nproceedings in respect of, that matter.\nThese arrangements may deal with keeping, and otherwise\nmanaging, such information.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7d-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7d-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7456fdf453155d301824a730a54e6eb796fa54a9c38a9c23a353861206571064",
      "skos:note": "Repeal subsection, substitute with arrangements for information sharing between jurisdictions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-7d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7D Subsection 23YUD(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into\narrangements with a responsible Minister of a participating\njurisdiction under which:\n\n(a) information from the DNA database system of the\nCommonwealth that may be relevant to the investigation of a\nmatter relating to the participating jurisdiction is to be\ntransmitted to the appropriate authority in that jurisdiction for\nthe purpose of the investigation of, or proceedings in respect\nof, that matter; and\n\n(b) information from a DNA database system of the participating\njurisdiction that may be relevant to the investigation of a\nmatter relating to the Commonwealth is to be transmitted to\nthe Commissioner for the purposes of the investigation of, or\nproceedings in respect of, that matter.\nThese arrangements may deal with keeping, and otherwise\nmanaging, such information.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7d-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7d"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7d-logic-alleninterval-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establish temporal intervals for information sharing.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Arrangements may deal with keeping and managing information.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Information sharing occurs within specified time frames."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Crimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) For the avoidance of doubt, this section does not preclude\nCrimTrac from entering into a memorandum of understanding or\nother arrangement, on behalf of the Commonwealth, with a\nparticipating jurisdiction in relation to:\n\n(a) transmission of information to or from the DNA database\nsystem of the Commonwealth, or a DNA database system of\nany participating jurisdiction; or\n\n(b) keeping, and otherwise managing, such information.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) For the avoidance of doubt, this section does not preclude\nCrimTrac from entering into a memorandum of understanding or\nother arrangement, on behalf of the Commonwealth, with a\nparticipating jurisdiction in relation to:\n\n(a) transmission of information to or from the DNA database\nsystem of the Commonwealth, or a DNA database system of\nany participating jurisdiction; or\n\n(b) keeping, and otherwise managing, such information.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-10-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f66665e2bd6ec2f2aa80d72143a9669dd7ef1f9c311081c8e3d2446928104b6",
      "skos:note": "Does not preclude CrimTrac from entering into a memorandum of understanding or other arrangement with participating jurisdictions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Crimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) For the avoidance of doubt, this section does not preclude\nCrimTrac from entering into a memorandum of understanding or\nother arrangement, on behalf of the Commonwealth, with a\nparticipating jurisdiction in relation to:\n\n(a) transmission of information to or from the DNA database\nsystem of the Commonwealth, or a DNA database system of\nany participating jurisdiction; or\n\n(b) keeping, and otherwise managing, such information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-10-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-10"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7E At the end of section 23YUD",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-7e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) In this section:\nCrimTrac means the CrimTrac Agency, established as an\nExecutive Agency by the Governor-General by order under\nsection 65 of the Public Service Act 1999.\ninvestigation of a matter means:\n\n(a) in relation to a participating jurisdiction:\n\n(i) an investigation of an offence against the law of that\njurisdiction; or\n\n(ii) an investigation of a missing person; or\n\n(iii) an investigation for the purpose of identifying a\ndeceased person; or\n\n(b) in relation to the Commonwealth:\n\n(i) an investigation of an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n\n(ii) an investigation of a missing person; or\n\n(iii) an investigation for the purpose of identifying a\ndeceased person.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(3) In this section:\nCrimTrac means the CrimTrac Agency, established as an\nExecutive Agency by the Governor-General by order under\nsection 65 of the Public Service Act 1999.\ninvestigation of a matter means:\n\n(a) in relation to a participating jurisdiction:\n\n(i) an investigation of an offence against the law of that\njurisdiction; or\n\n(ii) an investigation of a missing person; or\n\n(iii) an investigation for the purpose of identifying a\ndeceased person; or\n\n(b) in relation to the Commonwealth:\n\n(i) an investigation of an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n\n(ii) an investigation of a missing person; or\n\n(iii) an investigation for the purpose of identifying a\ndeceased person.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e232fb8b813c0ce9634098a4f2c33e22068e57b594e7a20b479c44e238f1ac39",
      "skos:note": "Definition of CrimTrac Agency and investigation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-7e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7E At the end of section 23YUD",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) In this section:\nCrimTrac means the CrimTrac Agency, established as an\nExecutive Agency by the Governor-General by order under\nsection 65 of the Public Service Act 1999.\ninvestigation of a matter means:\n\n(a) in relation to a participating jurisdiction:\n\n(i) an investigation of an offence against the law of that\njurisdiction; or\n\n(ii) an investigation of a missing person; or\n\n(iii) an investigation for the purpose of identifying a\ndeceased person; or\n\n(b) in relation to the Commonwealth:\n\n(i) an investigation of an offence against the law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n\n(ii) an investigation of a missing person; or\n\n(iii) an investigation for the purpose of identifying a\ndeceased person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e-logic-descriptionlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Class hierarchy for CrimTrac Agency",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "CrimTrac means the CrimTrac Agency, established as an Executive Agency by the Governor-General by order under section 65 of the Public Service Act 1999.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "CrimTrac is the CrimTrac Agency"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7e-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Investigation definition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "investigation of a matter means: ...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "investigation of a matter is defined as specified in this section"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7F Transitional provision for existing arrangements under",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-7f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "subsection 23YUD(1)\nAn arrangement that:\n\n(a) was entered into under subsection 23YUD(1) of the Crimes\nAct 1914 before the commencement of this item; and\n\n(b) was in force immediately before this commencement;\ncontinues in force after that commencement as if it had been entered\ninto under that subsection as amended by this Schedule.\n\nAmendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Schedule 1\nTechnical corrections of sentencing and parole provisions  Part 4\n\nCrimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003                 11",
      "skos:definition": "subsection 23YUD(1)\nAn arrangement that:\n\n(a) was entered into under subsection 23YUD(1) of the Crimes\nAct 1914 before the commencement of this item; and\n\n(b) was in force immediately before this commencement;\ncontinues in force after that commencement as if it had been entered\ninto under that subsection as amended by this Schedule.\n\nAmendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Schedule 1\nTechnical corrections of sentencing and parole provisions  Part 4\n\nCrimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003                 11",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-1-sec-7f-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1fed91bdaab372f391b03a14df82275fe4af0ac16933310d376a8cc9795a14c9",
      "skos:note": "Continues existing arrangements under subsection 23YUD(1) of the Crimes Act 1914 as amended by this Schedule."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-1-sec-7f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7F Transitional provision for existing arrangements under",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "subsection 23YUD(1)\nAn arrangement that:\n\n(a) was entered into under subsection 23YUD(1) of the Crimes\nAct 1914 before the commencement of this item; and\n\n(b) was in force immediately before this commencement;\ncontinues in force after that commencement as if it had been entered\ninto under that subsection as amended by this Schedule.\n\nAmendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Schedule 1\nTechnical corrections of sentencing and parole provisions  Part 4\n\nCrimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003                 11"
    },
