    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-2-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 At the end of section 29",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-2-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) If the Tribunal so requests, the Magistrate conducting a proceeding\nunder section 27 or 28 (or both) may permit examination or\ncross-examination of a person giving evidence or producing a\ndocument or other article at the proceeding, by:\n\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates; or\n\n(b) that person’s legal representative; or\n\n(c) the Tribunal’s legal representative;\nthrough a video link.\n\n(4) In this section:\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003                 17\nvideo link means a video and sound system that enables persons\nassembled in the Tribunal’s premises (or premises nominated by\nthe Tribunal) to see, hear and talk to persons assembled in a place\nin another country.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(3) If the Tribunal so requests, the Magistrate conducting a proceeding\nunder section 27 or 28 (or both) may permit examination or\ncross-examination of a person giving evidence or producing a\ndocument or other article at the proceeding, by:\n\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates; or\n\n(b) that person’s legal representative; or\n\n(c) the Tribunal’s legal representative;\nthrough a video link.\n\n(4) In this section:\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003                 17\nvideo link means a video and sound system that enables persons\nassembled in the Tribunal’s premises (or premises nominated by\nthe Tribunal) to see, hear and talk to persons assembled in a place\nin another country.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-2-sec-9-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003-sch-2-sec-9-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-enhancement-act-2003#sch-2-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 At the end of section 29",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) If the Tribunal so requests, the Magistrate conducting a proceeding\nunder section 27 or 28 (or both) may permit examination or\ncross-examination of a person giving evidence or producing a\ndocument or other article at the proceeding, by:\n\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates; or\n\n(b) that person’s legal representative; or\n\n(c) the Tribunal’s legal representative;\nthrough a video link.\n\n(4) In this section:\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Enhancement Act 2003                 17\nvideo link means a video and sound system that enables persons\nassembled in the Tribunal’s premises (or premises nominated by\nthe Tribunal) to see, hear and talk to persons assembled in a place\nin another country."
    },
